#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:648
msgid ""
"pub struct EngineSlot {\n"
"    current: RwLock<Arc<Engine>>,\n"
"    generation: AtomicU64,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn publish(&self, engine: Engine) {\n"
"    let fresh = Arc::new(engine);\n"
"    let previous = {\n"
"        let mut current =\n"
"            "
"self.current.write().unwrap_or_else(PoisonError::into_inner);\n"
"        std::mem::replace(&mut *current, fresh)\n"
"    };\n"
"    self.generation.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Release);\n"
"    // The old engine is dropped outside the lock (when this was its last "
"holder).\n"
"    drop(previous);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub struct EngineCache {\n"
"    generation: u64,\n"
"    engine: Option<Arc<Engine>>,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn refresh(&mut self, slot: &EngineSlot) -> &Engine {\n"
"    let generation = slot.generation();\n"
"    if self.generation != generation {\n"
"        // A publication between the load above and this clone labels a "
"newer\n"
"        // engine with an older generation; the next refresh simply loads "
"again.\n"
"        self.generation = generation;\n"
"        self.engine = None;\n"
"    }\n"
"    self.engine.get_or_insert_with(|| slot.load())\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"pub struct EngineSlot {\n"
"    current: RwLock<Arc<Engine>>,\n"
"    generation: AtomicU64,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn publish(&self, engine: Engine) {\n"
"    let fresh = Arc::new(engine);\n"
"    let previous = {\n"
"        let mut current =\n"
"            "
"self.current.write().unwrap_or_else(PoisonError::into_inner);\n"
"        std::mem::replace(&mut *current, fresh)\n"
"    };\n"
"    self.generation.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Release);\n"
"    // ⁧يُسقَط المحرك القديم خارج القفل (إذا كان هذا آخر حامل له).⁩\n"
"    drop(previous);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub struct EngineCache {\n"
"    generation: u64,\n"
"    engine: Option<Arc<Engine>>,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn refresh(&mut self, slot: &EngineSlot) -> &Engine {\n"
"    let generation = slot.generation();\n"
"    if self.generation != generation {\n"
"        // ⁧إذا وقع نشر بين التحميل أعلاه وهذا النسخ، وُسم محرك أحدث⁩\n"
"        // ⁧بجيل أقدم؛ والتحديث التالي يحمِّل من جديد ببساطة.⁩\n"
"        self.generation = generation;\n"
"        self.engine = None;\n"
"    }\n"
"    self.engine.get_or_insert_with(|| slot.load())\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:683
msgid ""
"The generation is stored with release ordering after the engine is in "
"place, and loaded with acquire ordering: a reader that sees a new "
"generation also sees the engine stored before it. The race named in the "
"comment is benign. If a publication lands between a reader's generation "
"load and its clone, the reader caches the newer engine under the older "
"generation number, and its next refresh notices the mismatch and loads "
"again. A reader can be one engine late for one request; it can never see "
"a half-built engine, because only complete engines are ever stored in the "
"slot."
msgstr ""
"يُخزَّن الجيل بترتيب release بعد أن يستقر المحرك في مكانه، ويُحمَّل "
"بترتيب acquire: القارئ الذي يرى جيلًا جديدًا يرى أيضًا المحرك المخزَّن "
"قبله. السباق المذكور في التعليق غير ضار. إذا وقع نشر بين تحميل القارئ "
"للجيل ونسخه، يخزن القارئ المحرك الأحدث مؤقتًا تحت رقم الجيل الأقدم، "
"ويلاحظ تحديثه التالي عدم التطابق فيحمِّل مرة أخرى. قد يتأخر القارئ محركًا "
"واحدًا لطلب واحد؛ لكنه لا يستطيع أبدًا أن يرى محركًا نصف مبني، لأن الموضع "
"لا يُخزَّن فيه إلا محركات كاملة."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:687
msgid ""
"Every engine a request reads is complete, and no engine is freed while "
"any request or connection cache holds it. The first holds because an "
"engine is built entirely before ``publish`` stores it; the second because "
"every reader holds an ``Arc``, and the engine is dropped only with its "
"last ``Arc``."
msgstr ""
"كل محرك يقرؤه طلب كامل، ولا يُحرَّر أي محرك ما دام أي طلب أو ذاكرة مؤقتة "
"لاتصال تحمله. يصح الأول لأن المحرك يُبنى بالكامل قبل أن تخزنه "
"``publish``؛ ويصح الثاني لأن كل قارئ يحمل ``Arc``، ولا يُسقط المحرك إلا "
"مع آخر ``Arc`` له."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:689
msgid ""
"Why a cache and not simply a lock? SID 0010 asked us to measure the read "
"cost with 16 threads and choose between ``RwLock<Arc<Engine>>`` and a "
"lock-free alternative in safe Rust. Reading through the lock takes the "
"lock word and the reference count, two cache lines that every core "
"writes. The generation, by contrast, is written once per publication and "
"otherwise only read, so each core keeps its copy:"
msgstr ""
"لماذا ذاكرة مؤقتة وليس قفلًا ببساطة؟ طلب منا SID 0010 أن نقيس تكلفة "
"القراءة مع 16 خيطًا ونختار بين ``RwLock<Arc<Engine>>`` وبديل بلا أقفال "
"بلغة Rust الآمنة. القراءة عبر القفل تأخذ كلمة القفل وعداد المراجع، وهما "
"سطرا ذاكرة مخبئية تكتب فيهما كل نواة. أما الجيل فيُكتب مرة واحدة لكل نشر "
"ويُقرأ فقط في غير ذلك، فتحتفظ كل نواة بنسختها منه:"

